Rāma nears Śr̥ṅgavērapura past broad Kōsala --- Beholds divine Gaṅgā loud with swans and crocodiles --- Halts by flowering iṅgudī tree for night --- Niṣāda chief Guha comes with kin and ministers --- Guha embraces Rāma and offers land and rule --- Guha brings rich foods arghya beds and fodder --- Rāma declines gifts as vowed bark-clad ascetic --- Takes only fodder and LakṣmaṆa-fetched water --- LakṣmaṆa washes feet of resting Rāma and Sītā --- Guha Sūta and LakṣmaṆa guard sleeping Rāma
